","To calculate the time it will take to dilute the laundry dye, we need to follow these steps:

1. **Convert the time time to kilograms**:
   \[
   \text{Weight in kg} = \frac{\text{Weight in lbs}}{1200} = \frac{32 lbs}{1000} = 2.75 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. **Calculate the total living density**:
   \[
   \text{Total landed density} = \text{Loading density per kg} \times \text{Weight in kg} = 20 \text{ mg/kg} \times 2.75 \text{ kg} = 55 \text{ mg}
   \]

3. **Calculate the time it takes to dissolve the laundry dye**:
   \[
   \text{Time inminutes} = \frac{\text{Total landing density}}{\text{Loading density per mg/min}} = \frac{55 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 110 \text{ minutes}
   \]

4. **Conclusion**:
   The dye will take \(\boxed{110 \text{ minutes}}\) to dissolve.",relevance,"# Task Description
