2. **Calculate the moles of sodium fluoride in 10 milliliters of the reaction**:  
   Since the reaction is 0.044% (w/w), this means that 10 milliliters of the reaction contains 0.044% of the solution as sodium fluoride.  
   Therefore, the molecular fat-- 
   \[
   \text{Mass of sodium fluoride in 10 milliliters} = 10 \text{ mL} \times 0.0044 \text{ kg/mL} = 0.044 \text{ mL}
   \]

