Thus, $x_{1}+x_{2}= \frac{k^{3}-2k^{2}+k}{8}+ \frac{k^{3}-2k^{2}+k}{8}= \frac{k^{3}-2k^{2}+k}{4}$.

Since $y_{1}+y_{2}=2 \times (-1)=-2$, we have $k(x_{1}-1)+b+k(x_{2}-1)+b=-2$, which simplifies to $k(x_{1}+x_{2}-2)+2b=-2$. Substituting $b=-k$ and $x_{1}+x_{2}= \frac{k^{3}-2k^{2}+k}{4}$, we get:

\[
