   - The center of the central sphere is at $(1, 1, 1)$.
   - The center of the sphere tangent to three faces of the cube is at $(r, r, r)$.
   - The remaining eight spheres are arranged symmetrically around the center sphere and are tangent to it and to two faces of the cube. The centers of these spheres are at $(r, r, 1)$, $(r, 1, r)$, $(r, 1, 1)$, $(1, r, r)$, $(1, r, 1)$, $(1, 1, r)$, $(1, 1, 1)$, $(1, 1, 1)$.

3. **Calculate the Distance Between Centers**:
