   \[
   \frac{d}{dt} \left( e^{-h(t) t} y \right) = g(t) e^{-h(t) t}
   \]
   Integrate both sides with respect to \( t \):
   \[
   e^{-h(t) t} y = \int g(t) e^{-h(t) t} \, dt + C
   \]

